# Premium Subtitle Localization

This project has a full subtitle-localization skill at
`skills/premium-subtitle-localization/SKILL.md` in this repo (or
wherever you copied the `skills/premium-subtitle-localization/` folder).
Read that file in full before subtitling anything — it covers the
find-or-transcribe step, the four-pass translation workflow (literal
draft, meaning-preserving rewrite, cultural adaptation, fluency/timing
polish), the automated validator plus agentic QA review, and the
no-re-encode video merge.

Quick reference:
- Step 0: get the video path, source/target language(s), genre/tone
  (comedy vs. drama vs. documentary changes translation priorities), and
  soft-sub vs. hardsub preference — ask briefly if unclear.
- `scripts/find_subtitles.py` before `scripts/transcribe.py` — never
  transcribe from audio if a usable subtitle file already exists.
- Translation is done by the agent itself, in four passes per
  `references/translation_workflow.md` — never delegate straight to a
  translation library/API, that produces exactly the flat literal output
  this skill exists to avoid.
- Always run `scripts/validate_srt.py` (mechanical QA) AND the
  `references/qa_review_checklist.md` review pass (meaning/quality QA)
  before merging — they check different things, both are required.
- `scripts/merge_subtitles.py` defaults to soft subtitles (`-c copy`, no
  re-encode); only use `--burn-in` if the target platform genuinely
  can't do subtitle tracks.
- Always run `scripts/verify_output.py` on the final file before telling
  the user it's ready.
